        "id": 1000086
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-08-11T02:19:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "My intent is that the plugin adds additional interfaces on the same log entry object and owns the implementation and lifecycle of those interfaces.\n\nFor example:\n\n/xyz/openbmc_project/logging/entry/123\n\nInterfaces:\n  xyz.openbmc_project.Logging.Entry\n  xyz.openbmc_project.Logging.Diagnostic.CPER\n\nIn this model, phosphor-logging remains responsible for the log entry lifecycle, while the plugin is responsible for creating and restoring any plugin-specific interfaces associated with that log entry.\n\nI wasn\u0027t intending for the plugin framework to require a separate daemon or a separate object hierarchy, \n\nI can clarify this in the document because the current wording around \"plugin-owned artifacts\" and \"plugin-defined interfaces\" may imply that the interfaces are always created somewhere outside of the log entry, which wasn\u0027t my intent.",
      "parentUuid": "b46326f4_5bfcc562",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 250,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 255,
        "endChar": 43
      },
