      "writtenOn": "2026-08-11T14:05:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In the extension code there is a Extensions::disableDefaultLogCaps() function that is used to basically delegate the ability to prune out old logs to the extension. \n\nWe have to do it based on more than just if informational or not, since all of the event logs from all of our host subsystems also get sent in.\n\nSo if you have a need, you could do something similar for the CPER stuff, but it sounds like CPERs are just for hardware errors so I wouldn\u0027t think are too common and the normal algorithm should be fine.",
      "parentUuid": "b38b7e27_9e6a7839",
